# Lead delivery — Web3Forms only.
#
# Every form is validated in the browser and then posted directly from the
# visitor's browser to https://api.web3forms.com/submit using the public
# access key that ships in code (lib/leadDelivery.ts —
# WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY). There is no server-side email route and no
# fallback relay of any kind; if Web3Forms does not accept a submission,
# the visitor sees an error and their entries are kept for retry.
#
# No environment variables are required for delivery. If the key is ever
# rotated in the Web3Forms dashboard, update WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY in
# lib/leadDelivery.ts.
#
# Delivery goes to the inbox bound to the access key in the Web3Forms
# dashboard (currently the office inbox).
